// Builder-pattern coverage fixture (typestate builders on every
// struct-shaped generated type, see `cratestack-core/src/builder.rs` and
// `cratestack-macros/src/builder.rs`). `BuilderWidget` deliberately mixes
// a required `String`, a required `Int`, and a nullable `String?` so the
// same model exercises:
//   * `CreateBuilderWidgetInput`'s builder — a mix of required + optional
//     setters, required ones gating `build()`.
//   * `UpdateBuilderWidgetInput`'s builder — every field optional (patch
//     wrapping), with `note`'s setter taking `Option<String>` so
//     `.note(Some(v))` sets and `.note(None)` clears (cratestack#567).
//   * `BuilderWidgetWhere` / `BuilderWidgetFindManyInput` — both
//     all-optional, non-generic builders.
//   * the `BuilderWidget` model struct's own builder (all fields
//     required except `note`).
//   * `BuilderWidgetSummary`'s view struct builder.
//
// `BuilderWidgetTags` (a `type` block, not a `model` field) covers the
// list-arity append setter (`.add_tags(item)` alongside the bulk
// `.tags(vec)` one — cratestack#661): `type` blocks aren't
// `datasource`-bound the way a `model` field is, so they're the one shape
// in this schema that can legally carry a scalar `String[]` field —
// `cratestack-parser`'s `validate_field_list_arity_support` rejects a
// list-valued scalar/enum *model* field on any schema with a `datasource`
// (no SQL bind representation for a list column), which `BuilderWidget`
// itself has. `scoped_builder_fields` (the `type`-block builder path) is
// always called with `wrap_for_patch = false` (see
// `crates/cratestack-macros/src/types.rs`), so it only exercises the
// non-patch append/bulk/unset shapes; the patch ("touched") shape is
// covered separately in `crates/cratestack-client/tests/builder_pattern.rs`,
// whose datasource-free fixture can put `tags String[]` directly on a
// model and get a real `Update{Model}Input`.

datasource db {
  provider = "sqlite"
  url = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

model BuilderWidget {
  id Int @id
  name String
  priority Int
  note String?
}

view BuilderWidgetSummary from BuilderWidget {
  id Int @id @from(BuilderWidget.id)
  name String @from(BuilderWidget.name)
  note String? @from(BuilderWidget.note)

  @@embedded_sql("SELECT id, name, note FROM builder_widgets")
}

type BuilderWidgetTags {
  tags String[]
}
